[2026-03-15T07:37:42.542Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RMwQbKLuHaKMhDuVnVr8z2","type":"tool_result","content":"# replay-cli Skill File\n\n**Name:** replay-cli\n\n**Description:** Record your application to gather performance data and debug issues. It enables users to install Replay CLI, record a session, upload and manage them.\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill helps users work with Replay CLI for recording browser sessions, uploading recordings, and managing authentication.\n\n## Key Installation & Setup\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun, then set up authentication by creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Main Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and record a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to Replay |\n| `list` | View all local recordings |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings locally |\n| `login` / `logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `info` | Display Replay dependencies info |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for a Workspace |\n\n## Core Workflow\n\nRecord a session at a URL, then upload the resulting recording using its ID. The CLI returns a shareable URL after successful upload.\n\n## MCP Integration\n\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications using the provided configuration command with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"316ad367-1475-485a-a257-5843849f2a92","uuid":"2c94a398-6f40-4de2-918c-0ffa6f492743","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# replay-cli Skill File\n\n**Name:** replay-cli\n\n**Description:** Record your application to gather performance data and debug issues. It enables users to install Replay CLI, record a session, upload and manage them.\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill helps users work with Replay CLI for recording browser sessions, uploading recordings, and managing authentication.\n\n## Key Installation & Setup\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun, then set up authentication by creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Main Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and record a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to Replay |\n| `list` | View all local recordings |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings locally |\n| `login` / `logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `info` | Display Replay dependencies info |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for a Workspace |\n\n## Core Workflow\n\nRecord a session at a URL, then upload the resulting recording using its ID. The CLI returns a shareable URL after successful upload.\n\n## MCP Integration\n\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications using the provided configuration command with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`.","durationMs":4729,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T07:37:42.938Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UyF4NRToQTAxJ1Lbcv1a6e","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Overview\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution history. The methodology emphasizes formulating questions, exploring relevant events, understanding causation, and supporting conclusions with gathered evidence.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe recording functions as a comprehensive database with two fundamental elements:\n- **Point:** A specific execution moment when a JavaScript statement runs or a significant event occurs\n- **Element:** A DOM element reference independent of time, existing throughout its lifecycle\n\n## Available Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when:\n- Error detection (UncaughtException, ReactException)\n- Timeline analysis (events, console messages, storage access, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (finding files, reading code with hit counts, searching patterns)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking (stack frames, control flow relationships)\n- State details (point descriptions, element inspection, component trees, expression evaluation)\n\n## Investigation Strategy\n\nEffective analysis involves locating relevant code, confirming its execution, examining execution details, and using the Logpoint tool to monitor expression values across multiple execution instances for anomalies."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"316ad367-1475-485a-a257-5843849f2a92","uuid":"1a0e715e-f0c5-48ae-ae7e-5e0e4fc5577f","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Overview\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution history. The methodology emphasizes formulating questions, exploring relevant events, understanding causation, and supporting conclusions with gathered evidence.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe recording functions as a comprehensive database with two fundamental elements:\n- **Point:** A specific execution moment when a JavaScript statement runs or a significant event occurs\n- **Element:** A DOM element reference independent of time, existing throughout its lifecycle\n\n## Available Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when:\n- Error detection (UncaughtException, ReactException)\n- Timeline analysis (events, console messages, storage access, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (finding files, reading code with hit counts, searching patterns)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking (stack frames, control flow relationships)\n- State details (point descriptions, element inspection, component trees, expression evaluation)\n\n## Investigation Strategy\n\nEffective analysis involves locating relevant code, confirming its execution, examining execution details, and using the Logpoint tool to monitor expression values across multiple execution instances for anomalies.","durationMs":4582,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
