[2026-03-15T07:38:15.233Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0144FooaQSJN7opo7AVuUd1v","type":"tool_result","content":"1211-- **Components**: CancelBookingModal\n1212-- **Initial state**: Cancel modal is open, a network error occurs during cancellation\n1213-- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel Booking\" and the request fails\n1214-- **Expected**: An error message is displayed in the modal (e.g., \"Failed to cancel booking. Please try again.\"). The modal remains open. The buttons become clickable again so the user can retry or dismiss.\n1215-\n1216-#### Test: CancelBookingModal cancelled trip persists in correct tab\n1217-- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard, TripsTabs\n1218-- **Initial state**: User cancels an upcoming booking via the modal\n1219-- **Action**: User switches to \"Past\" tab and back to \"Upcoming\" tab\n1220-- **Expected**: The cancelled trip still appears in the \"Upcoming\" tab (since the departure date is still in the future) with the \"Cancelled\" status badge. It is not duplicated across tabs.\n1221-\n1222-## Page: Explore\n1223-\n1224-### Components\n1225-- DestinationMap\n1226:- FlexibleDatesGrid\n1227-- DealsSection\n1228-\n1229-### DestinationMap\n1230-\n1231-#### Test: DestinationMap displays interactive map on Explore page\n1232-- **Components**: DestinationMap\n1233-- **Initial state**: User navigates to the Explore page\n1234-- **Action**: User observes the map area\n1235-- **Expected**: An interactive map is displayed showing a world/regional view. The map is centered based on the selected origin airport. The map supports zoom and pan interactions.\n1236-\n1237-#### Test: DestinationMap shows origin airport selector\n1238-- **Components**: DestinationMap\n1239-- **Initial state**: Explore page loads\n1240-- **Action**: User observes the origin selector above or within the map\n1241-- **Expected**: An origin airport selector is displayed (autocomplete input similar to the Search page). It defaults to a preferred/nearest airport or prompts the user to select one.\n--\n1276-- **Action**: Destinations are being fetched from the backend\n1277-- **Expected**: A loading indicator is shown on or near the map while destination data is being fetched. Once loaded, markers appear on the map.\n1278-\n1279-#### Test: DestinationMap shows empty state when no destinations available\n1280-- **Components**: DestinationMap\n1281-- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with an origin that has no available flights\n1282-- **Action**: User observes the map\n1283-- **Expected**: The map is displayed but with no destination markers. A message is shown indicating no destinations are currently available from this origin (e.g., \"No destinations found from this airport\").\n1284-\n1285-#### Test: DestinationMap origin can be changed repeatedly\n1286-- **Components**: DestinationMap\n1287-- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with origin set to LAX\n1288-- **Action**: User changes origin to JFK, observes results, then changes to LHR, observes results, then changes back to LAX\n1289-- **Expected**: Each origin change updates the map correctly with new destinations and prices. The map works correctly on each subsequent change without stale data or errors.\n1290-\n1291:### FlexibleDatesGrid\n1292-\n1293:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid displays calendar-style grid with prices\n1294:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1295-- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with an origin airport selected\n1296:- **Action**: User scrolls down to the Flexible Dates section\n1297-- **Expected**: A calendar-style grid is displayed showing departure dates as rows/columns. Each cell shows the lowest flight price for that departure date. The grid covers the upcoming weeks/months.\n1298-\n1299:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid cells are color-coded by price level\n1300:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1301:- **Initial state**: Explore page with flexible dates grid visible\n1302-- **Action**: User observes the grid cell colors\n1303-- **Expected**: Cells are color-coded: green for cheap prices, yellow for moderate prices, and red for expensive prices. The color coding provides a visual at-a-glance comparison of prices across dates.\n1304-\n1305:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid date range selector — Weekend trips\n1306:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1307:- **Initial state**: Explore page with flexible dates grid visible\n1308-- **Action**: User selects \"Weekend trips\" from the date range selector\n1309-- **Expected**: The grid updates to show prices specifically for weekend departure/return combinations (e.g., Friday–Sunday or Saturday–Monday). Cell prices reflect round-trip costs for weekend durations.\n1310-\n1311:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid date range selector — 1 week\n1312:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1313-- **Initial state**: Explore page with \"Weekend trips\" selected\n1314-- **Action**: User selects \"1 week\" from the date range selector\n1315-- **Expected**: The grid updates to show prices for 1-week trip durations. Each cell shows the lowest price for a round-trip departing on that date and returning 7 days later.\n1316-\n1317:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid date range selector — 2 weeks\n1318:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1319-- **Initial state**: Explore page with \"1 week\" selected\n1320-- **Action**: User selects \"2 weeks\" from the date range selector\n1321-- **Expected**: The grid updates to show prices for 2-week trip durations. Each cell shows the lowest price for a round-trip departing on that date and returning 14 days later.\n1322-\n1323:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid clicking a date cell initiates a search\n1324:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1325-- **Initial state**: Explore page with grid displayed, \"1 week\" selected, origin is LAX\n1326-- **Action**: User clicks on a specific date cell (e.g., March 20 showing \"$250\")\n1327-- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Search Results page with origin set to LAX, departure date set to March 20, return date set to March 27 (1 week later), and results displayed for that search.\n1328-\n1329:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid shows loading state while fetching price data\n1330:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1331-- **Initial state**: User changes origin airport or date range\n1332-- **Action**: Price data is being fetched\n1333-- **Expected**: The grid shows a loading skeleton or spinner while price data is being fetched. Once loaded, the grid populates with prices and color coding.\n1334-\n1335:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid updates when origin changes\n1336:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid, DestinationMap\n1337:- **Initial state**: Explore page with origin LAX and flexible dates grid showing prices\n1338-- **Action**: User changes the origin airport to JFK\n1339:- **Expected**: The flexible dates grid reloads and displays updated prices for flights from JFK. The color coding adjusts to the new price distribution.\n1340-\n1341:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid date range selector can be toggled repeatedly\n1342:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1343-- **Initial state**: Explore page with grid visible, \"Weekend trips\" selected\n1344-- **Action**: User switches to \"1 week\", then \"2 weeks\", then back to \"Weekend trips\"\n1345-- **Expected**: Each selection updates the grid correctly with appropriate prices and color coding. The grid responds correctly on every toggle without stale data.\n1346-\n1347:#### Test: FlexibleDatesGrid shows empty state when no prices available\n1348:- **Components**: FlexibleDatesGrid\n1349-- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with origin that has very limited flights\n1350-- **Action**: User observes the grid\n1351-- **Expected**: Cells with no available flights show a dash or \"N/A\" instead of a price. They are not color-coded or are displayed in a neutral/gray color to indicate no data.\n1352-\n1353-### DealsSection\n1354-\n1355-#### Test: DealsSection displays deal cards on Explore page\n1356-- **Components**: DealsSection\n1357-- **Initial state**: Explore page loaded with an origin airport selected\n1358-- **Action**: User scrolls down to the Deals section\n1359-- **Expected**: A section titled \"Deals\" (or similar) is displayed containing multiple deal cards. Each card shows a flight deal from the selected origin airport.\n1360-\n1361-#### Test: DealsSection deal card shows destination, dates, price, and savings\n1362-- **Components**: DealsSection\n1363-- **Initial state**: Explore page with deals visible"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01V6dRS2YhjhMYXLCNY2xCyH","session_id":"316ad367-1475-485a-a257-5843849f2a92","uuid":"f36c970d-ecb0-4427-a3b4-3d122d9f1bb0"}
